 \subsection{Reconstruction Pipeline}
 The inversion pipeline follows the sequence-to-text procedure introduced by Weiss \emph{et al.}~\cite{weiss2024prompt}. It first splits a length vector at observations equal to one and merges short chunks using a ten-unit minimum, with an additional list-boundary heuristic. These are heuristic segments rather than verified sentences. The first segment is decoded using \texttt{royweiss1/T5\_FirstSentences}; later segments use \texttt{royweiss1/T5\_MiddleSentences} with preceding reconstructed context. T5 generation uses stochastic sampling with top-$k=50$, temperature 1 and a two-token no-repeat n-gram constraint. Candidates are ranked by the transition log-probability sum.
